    INTERVALS.STANDARD cadence; the view performs NO HTTP. No direct transport in the view.
  Projection → UptimeMonitorProjector.project is a 1:1 port of the web derivations:
    services = SERVICE_KEYS.map(...) with status = components[key]?.status ?? 'unhealthy', failures =
    consecutiveFailures ?? 0, lastError ?? null, fixed order [database, mqtt, tesla_api,
    fleet_telemetry]; tone = statusVariant (ok/healthy→success, degraded→warning, else→danger);
    healthyCount = count(ok|healthy); overallStatus = data.status ?: 'unknown'. databaseSize/tableCount
    carried for the tall footer. Verified by an EXECUTED harness (43/43).
  Composition → WidgetShell chrome (Activity icon + "Uptime Monitor" title [hidden when compact] +
    freshness chip + refresh + optional Open) · Overall row ("Overall" label + "All OK"/status badge) ·
    compact(1×1) big healthyCount/total · standard service rows (StatusDot + label + OK/status badge) ·
    tall footer (top divider + "DB Size"/"Tables").
  Shared components → maps web @/components/ui + @/components/feedback to native:
    Badge→UptimeStatusBadge, StatusDot→UptimeStatusDot, ServiceRow→UptimeServiceRow,
    DataFreshness→UptimeFreshnessChip, Skeleton→TSSkeleton (shared), EmptyState→ContentUnavailableView.
    The badge/dot/rows are authored locally over the SAME tokens as the shared TSBadge so every label
    resolves through the per-surface UptimeMonitorStrings table (the shared components take only a
    LocalizedStringKey) — identical rationale to the sibling MQTTStatusWidget's chip/tile.
    Recharts→none / Leaflet→none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No system health data" +
    ContentUnavailableView) · error (icon + retry) · content · stale (warning freshness chip over
    cached content) · offline (muted freshness chip + cached content). Model phase resolution keeps
    cached content visible behind background refresh/errors; a hard failure with no cache → error.
  Breakpoints → isCompact = (cols == 1 && rows == 1), isTall = (rows >= 2) — verbatim web predicates.
    The view reads `size` directly (like the web component); the registry envelope is enforced by the
    grid through registration.clamp() (a tested utility), so the compact path stays faithful AND
    previewable/testable.
  i18n → all source titles/labels resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default)
